; The one variable: `layout_direction = 3` (RTL). color_picker.cpp never reads it: each container
; mirrors itself (box_container.cpp:184-192, grid_container.cpp:193-197,218-223), so all six rows
; swap ends. The picker is centred, so its own mirror (control.cpp:1785-1787) is the identity, and its
; width (354 / 3) splits the mode buttons exactly. No other RTL fixture nests six row shapes.

